title: No API::Docker::Secret / ::Config entity classes - secrets and configs list/inspect
  return raw
updated: 2026-08-27T15:55:35Z
---

Deliberate for now, recorded so the deviation is visible rather than
forgotten. The distribution invariant is that list and inspect return entity
objects (_wrap / _wrap_list); API::Docker::API::Secrets and
API::Docker::API::Configs return the daemon hashrefs instead, because ticket
#27 scoped the work to the two API classes only and there is no
API::Docker::Secret or API::Docker::Config to wrap into.

Both POD blocks say so explicitly under =method list and =method inspect, so
a caller is not surprised. Same shape as #31 for plugins.

If entity classes are added, note that a Secret carries no payload at all
while a Config carries Spec.Data as base64 - a Config entity is the natural
place to offer a decoded accessor, which the API class deliberately does not
do (it never rewrites a daemon response).
